# KITO Mastermind rules

## The invariant
A client's name, phone, email and notes belong to the agent who logged the lead.
No other member sees them without an active `lead_contact_grants` row.
THERE IS NO ADMIN OVERRIDE. If you are writing one, stop.

## Hard bans
1. `supabaseAdmin` only in src/server/admin, src/app/api/webhooks, src/app/api/cron, supabase/seed.ts.
2. The `leads` table only in src/server/repositories/leads.ts. Everything else uses `lead_pool` or the repository.
3. Money is `bigint` cents. Never a float, never a `number`.

## Always
- Authorization decisions live in src/server/policy.ts. Nowhere else.
- Server Actions: requireActor, Zod parse, fetch subject, policy check, mutate, audit, revalidate, return.
- Return `{ ok: true, data } | { ok: false, error, fieldErrors? }`.
- Lead reads return `LeadView`, a discriminated union on `contactVisible`.
- Every mutation touching access, money or roles writes an audit row in the same transaction.
- Every page works at 375px.
- Colours come from the @theme tokens. No arbitrary hex.

## Never
- No TODO, stub, placeholder or hardcoded sample data in committed code.
- No `any` in src/server. No `@ts-ignore`. No `console.log`.
- No client PII in notifications, emails, logs, audit metadata or Sentry.
- No new dependency without checking Section 3 of KITO-CURSOR-BUILD.md.

## Before finishing any task
Run: pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test
The leak test (tests/e2e/leak.spec.ts) must never be skipped.
